{"status":"OK","data":{"id":5294,"identifier":"7E4/DST7ZY","persistentUrl":"https://doi.org/10.21410/7E4/DST7ZY","protocol":"doi","authority":"10.21410","publisher":"data.sciencespo","publicationDate":"2023-07-10","storageIdentifier":"file://10.21410/7E4/DST7ZY","metadataLanguage":"fr","latestVersion":{"id":4620,"datasetId":5294,"datasetPersistentId":"doi:10.21410/7E4/DST7ZY","storageIdentifier":"file://10.21410/7E4/DST7ZY","versionNumber":5,"versionMinorNumber":0,"versionState":"RELEASED","UNF":"UNF:6:kLSFkWXE96trhkrKo8wkZw==","lastUpdateTime":"2026-07-03T13:27:28Z","releaseTime":"2026-07-03T13:27:28Z","createTime":"2026-07-03T13:27:25Z","publicationDate":"2023-07-10","citationDate":"2023-07-10","license":{"name":"CC BY-SA 4.0","uri":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","iconUri":"https://licensebuttons.net/l/by-sa/4.0/88x31.png"},"termsOfAccess":"En téléchargeant ces données, vous vous engagez à respecter les Conditions générales d'utilisation de cet entrepôt de données.","fileAccessRequest":true,"metadataBlocks":{"citation":{"displayName":"Citation Metadata","name":"citation","fields":[{"typeName":"title","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"French Election Study 2022, Vague 3 (ELIPSS 2022)"},{"typeName":"author","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Briatte, François"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"European School of Political and Social Sciences (ESPOL)"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0001-6494-9774"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Dormagen, Jean-Yves"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Centre d'Études Politiques et Sociales (CEPEL)"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Gonthier, Frédéric"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"PACTE"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0002-8536-6487"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Gougou, Florent"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"PACTE"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0003-3298-4262"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Haute, Tristan"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Centre d'Études et de Recherches Administratives Politiques (CERAPS)"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0002-2065-420X"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Mayer, Nonna"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Centre d'Études Européennes, Sciences Po Paris"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0002-6610-8896"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Persico, Simon"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Centre Emile Durkheim"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0002-2166-7870"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sauger, Nicolas"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sciences Po, Centre de données socio-politiques (CDSP), CNRS"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0001-5178-195X"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Soubiran, Thomas"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Centre d'Études et de Recherches Administratives Politiques (CERAPS)"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0001-8531-8488"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Tiberj, Vincent"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Centre Emile Durkheim"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0001-5048-7855"}}]},{"typeName":"datasetContact","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"datasetContactName":{"typeName":"datasetContactName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sciences Po, Centre de données socio-politiques (CDSP), CNRS"},"datasetContactEmail":{"typeName":"datasetContactEmail","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"info.cdsp@sciencespo.fr"}}]},{"typeName":"dsDescription","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Dans la lignée des précédentes éditions de la French election study (FES), le panel FES-2022 représente une contribution à la compréhension des dynamiques électorales pendant la séquence électorale française de 2022 (élection présidentielle an avril et élections législatives au mois de juin). Le projet est collaboratif et comprend cinq vagues d’interrogation en tout, de novembre 2021 à juillet 2022. Il s’inscrit dans la programmation plus générale du panel Elipss.\nCette troisième vague de FES-2022 a été réalisée du 31 mars au 28 avril 2022 et donc pendant les votes pour l’élection présidentielle. L’enquête ne répète pas les modules précédents mais s’intéresse à la perception de la démocratie, au souhait sur le fonctionnement des institutions et à l’opinion sur la possibilité d’un vote à distance. L’enquête comprend également une batterie sur la perception de différents groupes sociaux ou politiques. Elle s’intéresse enfin à la perception des autres pays et de l’Union européenne, à la guerre en Ukraine et aux attitudes économiques des répondants."}},{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"As in previous editions of the French election study (FES), the FES-2022 panel represents a contribution to the understanding of electoral dynamics during the French electoral sequence of 2022 (presidential election in April and legislative elections in June). The project is collaborative and comprises a total of five waves of questioning, from November 2021 to July 2022. It is part of the wider Elipss panel program. \nThis third wave of FES-2022 was carried out from March 31 to April 28, 2022 and therefore during the votes for the presidential election. The survey does not repeat the previous modules but focuses on the perception of democracy, the wish on the functioning of institutions and the opinion on the possibility of remote voting. The survey also includes a battery on the perception of different social or political groups. Finally, it looks at the perception of other countries and of the European Union, the war in Ukraine and the economic attitudes of respondents."}}]},{"typeName":"subject","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Social Sciences"]},{"typeName":"keyword","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"ÉLECTIONS PRÉSIDENTIELLES (ELSST)"},"keywordVocabularyURI":{"typeName":"keywordVocabularyURI","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://elsst.ukdataservice.ac.uk/"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"INSTITUTIONS POLITIQUES (ELSST)"},"keywordVocabularyURI":{"typeName":"keywordVocabularyURI","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://elsst.ukdataservice.ac.uk/"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"CANDIDATS ET CANDIDATES POUR LA PRÉSIDENTIELLE (ELSST)"},"keywordVocabularyURI":{"typeName":"keywordVocabularyURI","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://elsst.ukdataservice.ac.uk/"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"INSTITUTIONS POLITIQUES"},"keywordVocabulary":{"typeName":"keywordVocabulary","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"ELSST"},"keywordVocabularyURI":{"typeName":"keywordVocabularyURI","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://elsst.cessda.eu/id/6/7ace6cfc-2e46-410e-b809-f48499616be3"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"ÉLECTIONS PRÉSIDENTIELLES"},"keywordVocabulary":{"typeName":"keywordVocabulary","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"ELSST"},"keywordVocabularyURI":{"typeName":"keywordVocabularyURI","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://elsst.cessda.eu/id/6/ecdad1a6-5645-44c5-b62b-8a3a9999fe57"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"CANDIDATS ET CANDIDATES POUR LA PRÉSIDENTIELLE"},"keywordVocabulary":{"typeName":"keywordVocabulary","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"ELSST"},"keywordVocabularyURI":{"typeName":"keywordVocabularyURI","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://elsst.cessda.eu/id/6/71ed0874-dbcf-4492-a051-596acde6571b"}}]},{"typeName":"topicClassification","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"topicClassValue":{"typeName":"topicClassValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"Politics"},"topicClassVocabURI":{"typeName":"topicClassVocabURI","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://elsst.ukdataservice.ac.uk/"}}]},{"typeName":"publication","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"publicationCitation":{"typeName":"publicationCitation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"French Electoral Study 2017"},"publicationIDType":{"typeName":"publicationIDType","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"doi"},"publicationIDNumber":{"typeName":"publicationIDNumber","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"10.21410/7E4/2XE05I"},"publicationURL":{"typeName":"publicationURL","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://data.sciencespo.fr/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.21410/7E4/2XE05I"}},{"publicationCitation":{"typeName":"publicationCitation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"French Electoral Study 2012"},"publicationIDType":{"typeName":"publicationIDType","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"doi"},"publicationIDNumber":{"typeName":"publicationIDNumber","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"10.21410/7E4/B3SXDT"},"publicationURL":{"typeName":"publicationURL","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://data.sciencespo.fr/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.21410/7E4/B3SXDT"}},{"publicationCitation":{"typeName":"publicationCitation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"French Electoral Study 2007"},"publicationIDType":{"typeName":"publicationIDType","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"doi"},"publicationIDNumber":{"typeName":"publicationIDNumber","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"10.21410/7E4/XKHCPM"},"publicationURL":{"typeName":"publicationURL","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"https://data.sciencespo.fr/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.21410/7E4/XKHCPM"}}]},{"typeName":"language","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["French"]},{"typeName":"producer","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"producerName":{"typeName":"producerName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sciences Po, Centre de données socio-politiques (CDSP), CNRS"}}]},{"typeName":"productionPlace","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Sciences Po 27 rue Saint-Guillaume 75337 Paris cedex 07"]},{"typeName":"distributor","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"distributorName":{"typeName":"distributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sciences Po, Centre de données socio-politiques (CDSP), CNRS"}}]},{"typeName":"depositor","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sciences Po, Centre de données socio-politiques (CDSP), CNRS"},{"typeName":"dateOfDeposit","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2023-07-10"},{"typeName":"dateOfCollection","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"dateOfCollectionStart":{"typeName":"dateOfCollectionStart","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2022-03-31"},"dateOfCollectionEnd":{"typeName":"dateOfCollectionEnd","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2022-04-27"}}]},{"typeName":"kindOfData","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Numeric"]},{"typeName":"series","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"seriesName":{"typeName":"seriesName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"ELIPSS"},"seriesInformation":{"typeName":"seriesInformation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"LIPSS est un panel Internet représentatif de la population résidant en France métropolitaine. Les panélistes sont sélectionnés aléatoirement. Ils répondent tous les mois en ligne à des enquêtes élaborées par des chercheurs. Les informations démographiques et socio-économiques proviennent de l’enquête annuelle. Pour la phase pilote du projet, un premier échantillon constitué de 1 039 panélistes a été recruté en 2012. En 2016, 2 514 individus viennent compléter les 817 de la phase pilote toujours présents dans le dispositif. En 2019, le modèle du dispositif évolue, et 1 400 panélistes sur les 2 400 encore présents acceptent de continuer leur participation. En 2020, un troisième recrutement de 900 personnes vient porter la taille du panel à 2 300 personnes."}}]}]},"geospatial":{"displayName":"Geospatial Metadata","name":"geospatial","fields":[{"typeName":"geographicCoverage","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"country":{"typeName":"country","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"France"}}]},{"typeName":"geographicUnit","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["France métropolitaine (hors Corse)"]}]},"socialscience":{"displayName":"Social Science and Humanities Metadata","name":"socialscience","fields":[{"typeName":"unitOfAnalysis","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Individual"]},{"typeName":"universe","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Population résidant en France métropolitaine (hors Corse) : - ayant plus de 18 ans le 1er janvier 2020 ; - habitant en résidence ordinaire ; - lisant suffisamment le français pour répondre à un questionnaire auto-administré."]},{"typeName":"timeMethod","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"Longitudinal.Panel.Continuous"},{"typeName":"dataCollector","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sciences Po, Centre de données socio-politiques (CDSP), CNRS"},{"typeName":"frequencyOfDataCollection","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Les enquêtes ELIPSS sont généralement mensuelles."},{"typeName":"samplingProcedure","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"Probability.Cluster.StratifiedRandom"},{"typeName":"collectionMode","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.CAWI"]},{"typeName":"researchInstrument","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"Questionnaire.Structured"},{"typeName":"dataCollectionSituation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Le panel ELIPSS est composé d'individus recrutés à partir de trois échantillons différents. Pour les deux premiers, recrutés respectivement en 2012 et 2016, deux tirages d'échantillon ont été réalisés par la division Sondage de l'Insee dans l'enquête annuelle du recensement (vagues 2011 et 2014) formant un ensemble de 13 500 logements. Les tirages de ces échantillons ont été réalisés de façon similaire (stratifié à plusieurs degrés et en grappes). Un seul individu a été tiré au sort dans chaque logement. La documentation des pondérations présente plus en détail la formation de l'échantillon. Le plan de sondage n'a pas été caractérisé : aucun estimateur de variance n'est conseillé pour produire un intervalle de confiance dans une inférence sous le plan. À l'issue du deuxième recrutement, 2 514 nouveaux individus ont accepté de participer au panel et ont reçu une tablette tactile pour répondre aux enquêtes (la réception de la tablette est le critère indispensable pour être défini comme un panéliste ELIPSS). Ils s'ajoutent aux 817 panélistes du pilote : 3 331 individus font partie du panel ELIPSS en avril 2016. Le troisième recrutement a eu lieu en 2020, à partir d'une base d'individus, le fichier Fidéli. Ce recrutement s'est étalé sur l'année 2020, et a permis de recruter près d'un millier de nouveaux panélistes. Ces panélistes ont été recrutés pour partie par les facteurs de la Poste, pour partie en face-à-face, et pour partie, à cause des restrictions sanitaires, par téléphone."},{"typeName":"actionsToMinimizeLoss","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Les actions des gestionnaires de panel en parallèle peuvent impacter le taux de réponse."},{"typeName":"weighting","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"La documentation des pondérations présente plus en détail  : <a href=\"https://hal.science/hal-03863489\"=\"_blank\">la procédure de redressement et l'utilisation des pondérations</a>"},{"typeName":"responseRate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Taux de réponse : 85.4% sur les 1 890 invités* à répondre à l'enquête. Sont invités à participer à l'enquête les panélistes en mesure d'y répondre (ne se sont pas déclarés absents pendant toute la durée du terrain, matériel en état, etc.)."}]}},"files":[{"label":"Documentation_FES2022_V3.pdf","restricted":false,"version":1,"datasetVersionId":4620,"categories":["Documentation"],"dataFile":{"id":5302,"persistentId":"doi:10.21410/7E4/DST7ZY/0U5PS9","pidURL":"https://doi.org/10.21410/7E4/DST7ZY/0U5PS9","filename":"Documentation_FES2022_V3.pdf","contentType":"application/pdf","filesize":721750,"categories":["D